# `core`'s own root file. The filesystem is the source of truth for what a
# *local* build compiles (see docs/10-modules-and-linkage.md's "Eager local
# discovery") -- every submodule here is included in `core`'s own build
# (`just build-core`) whether or not it's imported below. These imports
# still matter for one, narrower reason: `for`-extension discovery
# (`Driver::discover_extensions`) walks `core`'s tree via its *own* import
# graph, from this file, unconditionally -- for a consumer that `--extern`s
# `core` (the ordinary case), not just when `core` is compiled standalone --
# so a submodule missing here would have any `for`-block it declares
# silently invisible to every consumer, regardless of local/extern.

import cmp;
import default;
import glue;
import iterator;
import numerics;
import option;
import slices;
import strings;
